     "source": "CDISC"
    },
    {
     "definition": "Individuals with origins in any of the original peoples of North, Central, and South America, including, for example, Navajo Nation, Blackfeet Tribe of the Blackfeet Indian Reservation of Montana, Native Village of Marrow Inupiat Traditional Government, Nome Eskimo Community, Aztec, and Maya.",
